Dependencies
------------
The source dependency declarations are in backend/requirements.txt and
frontend/package.json. frontend/package-lock.json records the frontend
dependency versions. tools/packaging/requirements-lock.txt records the
separate Windows build environment.

MinerU is an optional document-parsing dependency. Its installed license
includes additional terms beyond the standard Apache-2.0 text. Refer to
the exact distribution's LICENSE.md before redistributing that component.
The Windows license collector checks that text against a pinned hash.

The Windows packaging specification excludes mineru_llama_cpp, GGUF
runtime support, Gradio and the other packages listed in its excludes
setting. They must not be inferred to be bundled merely because they
appear in the build environment's dependency lock.

Distribution notices
--------------------
tools/packaging/collect_licenses.py collects the license texts for the
Windows distribution from the build environment, the packaging
specification and the vendored license texts under
tools/packaging/licenses-vendor/. Its generated inventory records the
component names, license sources and hashes. It is derived from the build
environment, dependency lock and packaging exclusions, rather than the
actual frozen module inventory; build-only components may appear.

Windows installers include LICENSE, NOTICE and a licenses directory.
Consult that generated directory for the collected license materials and
verify them against the actual distribution. The collector's PASS covers
its explicit file and hash assertions, not complete license compliance.

The vendored texts retain their provenance notes. The cobble text is a
BSD template prepared from upstream declarations, not a retrieved
upstream license file. Other notes referring to master/main are not yet
bound to immutable source revisions for each listed package version.
The proxy_tools upstream text and wheel declaration differ; the retained
text also contains an unusual concatenation. These require further
version-specific source verification before claiming complete coverage.

Model weights are distributed separately from this source repository.
tools/packaging/models-manifest.txt records the expected ONNX files,
sizes and hashes. A file hash is an integrity check, not a license grant;
redistribution also requires the terms and provenance of the exact model
files. Model terms are not covered by this project's Apache-2.0 license.
